<title>UK: HSBC sets new high after strong HK market.</title>
<headline>HSBC sets new high after strong HK market.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in HSBC Holdings Plc set a record high on Wednesday in the wake of a strong showing by shares in Hong Kong, where half its stock is owned, traders said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 29p at 13.12-1/2 stg by 0953 GMT, after earlier touching a peak of 13.14 stg -- surpassing the previous high of 13.13 stg set October 24.  </p>
<p>&quot;Hong Kong has been up sharply and given the strength of the market there the rise in HSBC is not particularly amazing,&quot; said one senior trader.</p>
<p>In Hong Kong,the Hang Seng index rose 2.2 percent to close at a record 12,775.47.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
